IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ss-types`
IMPORT `ss-general`
IMPORT `ss-rates`
IMPORT `ss-entitlement`
IMPORT `ss-commencement`

-- Social Security Act 2018, main benefits — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For a person applying for a main benefit: are they entitled, at what
--    weekly rate after the income test, and from what day?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Benefit position` HAS
    `entitled`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `weekly rate`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `commences on`                                      IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref ss 16-36, 40, 313, 316; Schedules 2, 4
@export default A person's position on a main benefit under the Social Security Act 2018 (NZ): whether they are entitled to jobseeker support, sole parent support or the supported living payment (ss 16-36, 40); the weekly rate after the income test (s 17, Schedules 2 and 4); and the day it commences after the stand-down (s 316). The rate and commencement are given only where the person is entitled. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN b IS A `Main benefit`  @desc The benefit applied for
      a IS AN Applicant  @desc Birth date, citizenship or visa, residence, other benefits, dependent children and relationship
      j IS A `Jobseeker facts`  @desc The jobseeker facts
      s IS A `Sole parent facts`  @desc The sole parent facts
      l IS A `Supported living facts`  @desc The supported living payment facts
      r IS A `Rate facts`  @desc The base rate, income test and weekly income
      c IS A `Commencement facts`  @desc Entitlement date, end of employment, application date and stand-down
GIVETH A `Benefit position`
`the benefit position for` b `, applicant` a `, jobseeker facts` j `, sole parent facts` s `, supported living facts` l `, rate facts` r `, commencement facts` c MEANS
    `Benefit position` WITH
        `entitled`      IS entitled
        `weekly rate`   IS IF entitled THEN `the weekly rate of` b `, rate facts` r ELSE 0
        `commences on`  IS IF entitled THEN JUST (`the day the benefit commences, benefit` b `, facts` c) ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        entitled MEANS `is entitled to` b `, applicant` a `, jobseeker facts` j `, sole parent facts` s `, supported living facts` l `, rate facts` r `, on` (c's `became entitled on`)
